ath11k: do not panic the host when a radio firmware asserts

ath11k_core_ssr_notifier_cb() ends in BUG_ON(1) unless ab->fw_recovery_support
is set, and the AHB path never set it (only pci.c did, to false). On a
multi-PD IPQ5018 any QCN6122 (UserPD) firmware assert therefore takes down the
whole AP instead of just the radio - a remote reboot loop with no diagnostics.
Set it in the AHB probe so the SSR path is used instead.

--- backports-20210222_001-5.4.164-b157d2276.orig/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.c
+++ backports-20210222_001-5.4.164-b157d2276/drivers/net/wireless/ath/ath11k/ahb.c
@@ -966,6 +966,10 @@
 	ab->hw_rev = (enum ath11k_hw_rev)of_id->data;
 	ab->fw_mode = ATH11K_FIRMWARE_MODE_NORMAL;
 	ab->enable_cold_boot_cal = ath11k_cold_boot_cal;
+	/* A UserPD radio firmware assert must not panic the host. Without
+	 * this, ath11k_core_ssr_notifier_cb() hits BUG_ON(1) and the whole
+	 * AP goes down on any radio firmware crash. */
+	ab->fw_recovery_support = true;
 	ab->userpd_id = userpd_id;
 
 	mutex_lock(&dev_init_lock);
